cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CHAKRAVYUH: policy fuzzing for emergency telecommunications governance"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ranny
    family-names: Nayyar
    affiliation: Quantum QAI
repository-code: "https://github.com/"   # set on publication
abstract: >-
  CHAKRAVYUH replays a real cyclone timeline under multiple encoded legal regimes
  to find where emergency telecommunications obligations fail to fire in time.
  Six role-bound agents propose actions; a deterministic policy engine with no
  model in it decides their legality against clause-level records of the governing
  instruments. Property violations are classified into policy, coordination,
  execution and standards gaps, each citing the clause responsible, and every step
  is written to a hash-chained ledger. Aligned with ITU-T Y.3172, Y.3173 and Y.3181
  and mapped to the ITU AI Readiness 2.0 framework.
keywords:
  - emergency telecommunications
  - policy simulation
  - multi-agent systems
  - property-based testing
  - ITU-T Y.3172
  - disaster management
license: Apache-2.0
date-released: "2026-10-10"
